        "text": {
            "description_html": "<b>Baldwin 6795 Oval Mortise Lexington, formerly Wilmington, Entry Set with 5025 Egg Knob</b>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nThe Baldwin made Lexington 6795 Entrance Set has a classic design that will look beautiful in any traditional home. The 5025 Egg Knob mirrors the oval shape of this mortise entryset. The tough PVD Polished Brass Finish is backed by a lifetime warranty and is great for harsh climates such as extreme heat or salty environments. It will fit 1-3/8\" or 1-3/4\" door thicknesses and with backsets of 2-1/2\" or 2-3/4\".\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\nMortise locks have been, and still are, the established norm for Europe and much of the rest of the world. In the early 1960’s Baldwin brought residential mortise locks to America. They ‘founded’ the residential mortise industry and continue to be the leader – so much so that their competitors have bought Baldwin locks for their own products.\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Also Available: Matching <a href=\"/products/egg-knobset-baldwin-5025\"><b>Baldwin 5025 Egg Knobset</b></a></p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>Features</b> of the Traditional 6795 Lexington Door Entrance Set:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Certified by Underwriters Laboratories (UL) for use on fire doors up to three-hour rating.</li>\r\n<li>Made of solid forged brass.</li>\r\n<li>Heavy-duty mortise lock body</li>\r\n<li>Forged brass mechanical.</li>\r\n<li>One inch throw deadbolt with two hardened inserts.</li>\r\n<li>Reinforced steel security strike with three inch screws.</li>\r\n<li>Comes packaged with two keys.</li>\r\n<li><b>Lifetime Limited Warranty</b> on workmanship, materials, operation and finish.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p><b>Specifications</b> of the Classic Estate Collection Lexington Entryset:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Finish: <b>PVD Polished Brass</b></li>\r\n<li>Interior Trim: 5026 Knob</li>\r\n<li>Length: 10\"</li>\r\n<li>Width: 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li>Thickness: .281\"</li>\r\n<li>Knob Length: 2-1/2\"</li>\r\n<li>Knob Width: 1-1/2\"</li>\r\n<li>Overall Projection: 2.87\"</li>\r\n<li>Door Thickness: 1-3/4\" or 1-3/8\"</li>\r\n<li>Backset:  2-1/2\" or 2-3/4\"</li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/BAL-6546.pdf?v=1691094973\" target=\"new\"><b>Lexington Entry Set Specification Sheet (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n<li><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/BAL-estate_mortise_dimensions.pdf?v=1691094972\" target=\"new\"><b>Mortise Box Specification Sheet (PDF)</b></a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<b>When Selecting a Function:</b>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><b>Full Dummy Set:</b> Trim for non-working doors. It does not latch and does not lock. Usually used as matching trim for the non-working side of double doors.</li>\r\n<li><b>Single Cylinder:</b> From the exterior, a knob operates the entrance set latch and a key operates the deadbolt. From the inside, a thumbturn unlocks the deadbolt and a knob operates the latch.</li>\r\n<li><b>Double Cylinder:</b> From the exterior, a knob operates entrance set latch; while from the interior, it is operated by a knob. The deadbolt is operated by a key from both the inside and the outside.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</p>\r\n\r\n<p>\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0766/1489/3857/files/BAL-3-Functions-entryset.jpg?v=1704354505\" width=\"350\" height=\"125\" border=\"0\" alt=\"Baldwin Functions Chart\">\r\n</p>",
